      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{4a-6b+9c}{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4a-6b+9c}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}-\\frac{6b}{3}+\\frac{9c}{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}-\\frac{6}{3}\\cdot b+\\frac{9}{3}\\cdot c & = \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}-2b+3c & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
